### Orbit.Api manual test requests.
### Works with Visual Studio's built-in .http endpoint explorer and VS Code's "REST Client" extension.
### Run against the Docker Compose stack (`docker compose up --build`) unless you change @baseUrl below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Register a new account. Change the email/userName if you run this more than once - both are unique
### per account.
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "userName": "testuser",
  "displayName": "Test User",
  "password": "correct horse battery staple"
}

### Log in with the same credentials - emailOrUserName accepts either one. Copy the "token" value from
### the response into @token below (VS Code's REST Client can do this automatically via
### {{login.response.body.$.token}}; if your tool doesn't support that, paste it in by hand).
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailOrUserName": "testuser",
  "password": "correct horse battery staple"
}

### Everything below requires a token from register/login above.
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Should be empty ([]) the first time.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a note.
# @name createNote
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "First note",
  "content": "Created through requests.http"
}

### List notes again - the one just created should be the only entry.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token at all, this should now return 401 (previously it returned notes for everyone).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes

### Should be empty ([]) the first time.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a task list. isCompleted on the task list itself is derived server-side from whether every
### item is completed, so it's ignored here even if you set it - see the "Tasks" section in README.md.
# @name createTaskList
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries",
  "items": [
    { "description": "Buy milk", "dueDateUtc": "2026-08-20T18:00:00Z", "isCompleted": false },
    { "description": "Buy bread", "dueDateUtc": null, "isCompleted": false }
  ]
}

### List task lists again - the one just created should be the only entry.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Fetch it by id (VS Code's REST Client can pick the id up automatically via
### {{createTaskList.response.body.$}}; if your tool doesn't support that, paste it in by hand).
@taskListId = {{createTaskList.response.body.$}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskListId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update it - checking off both items should flip isCompleted to true on the task list itself.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskListId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries",
  "items": [
    { "description": "Buy milk", "dueDateUtc": "2026-08-20T18:00:00Z", "isCompleted": true },
    { "description": "Buy bread", "dueDateUtc": null, "isCompleted": true }
  ]
}

### Fetch it again - isCompleted should now be true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskListId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
